+The full design lifecycle in one skill: Context Gathering → Ceremony → Frame →
+Research → Evaluate → Solution → Review Gate → Address Feedback → Publish →
+Completion. Routes to each stage reference in order (or directly to one stage,
+on request), stopping once per phase for developer confirmation (two stops —
+sign-off, then commit — except Review Gate/Address Feedback, which wait on the
+real external MR approval state). Replaces the former separate `design-frame`,
 `design-research`, `design-evaluate`, `design-solution`, `design-review-gate`,
-`design-review`, `design-address-feedback`, `design-publish` skills — those stages
-now live under this one skill's `references/`.
+`design-review`, `design-address-feedback`, `design-publish` skills — those
+stages now live under this one skill's `references/`.
+
+**Context Gathering and Ceremony are separate stages**, mirroring `dev`'s own
+split: Context Gathering resolves the ticket/local ID, fetches tracker
+context, and identifies the design track/subfolder — read-only, and it
+creates the story folder and `design/Report.md`. Ceremony is the only stage
+that mutates the tracker or checks out a branch. Frame then writes the
+framing content (`design/00 Frame.md`) using what Context Gathering resolved.
+This replaces the earlier (4.x/5.x) design where Frame did all three jobs
+itself.
+
+Completion owns archiving, tracker sync, and the final commit/PR, separated
+out of what Publish used to do alone, and it is also where a design
+**declined** at Address Feedback ends up — Publish is skipped for a decline,
+since there are no permanent docs to update.
+
+Design-lifecycle artifacts live under `{{DESIGN_STORIES_ROOT}}` —
+`docs/Stories/design/` for a Project design, `docs/Stories/product-design/`
+for a Product design, identified by Context Gathering as part of track
+resolution and never re-derived. Active at `{{DESIGN_STORIES_ROOT}}[{TICKET}] {name}/`,
+archived at `{{DESIGN_STORIES_ROOT}}approved/[{TICKET}] {name}/` or
+`{{DESIGN_STORIES_ROOT}}declined/[{TICKET}] {name}/` — either way separate
+from the dev skill's `docs/Stories/[{TICKET}] {name}/impl/`, which is not
+namespaced this way, and the two design roots never mix in the same parent
+folder.
 
 `design-review` is retired as a standalone skill; its parameterized WAF assessment
